WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.260
Open calendar time is not the same as usable capacity.

2
00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:10.520
A free hour after five meetings may not support the same work as a protected hour before the day becomes noisy.

3
00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:16.700
Prioritization improves when the plan accounts for attention and energy, not only available minutes.

4
00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:20.240
Every hour is not equal for every task.

5
00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:26.120
Deep work is focused effort on demanding tasks that require sustained attention.

6
00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:34.380
It includes design, analysis, writing, troubleshooting, strategy, code review, learning, and hard decisions.

7
00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:41.120
Shallow work is lower-intensity work such as routine messages, scheduling, simple approvals, cleanup, and status updates.

8
00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:46.820
Shallow work is necessary, but it becomes damaging when it fragments the time needed for deep work.

9
00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:48.460
Energy windows vary.

10
00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:50.800
Some people think most clearly early.

11
00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:53.140
Others handle collaboration better later.

12
00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:56.680
The point is not to force every person into one pattern.

13
00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:02.140
The point is to observe when different kinds of work go best and schedule accordingly where possible.

14
00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:08.000
Demanding work should be placed in stronger attention windows when the system gives enough control to do that.

15
00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:11.480
Batching administrative tasks helps protect focus.

16
00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:21.740
Instead of checking every message the instant it arrives, a person or team can create response windows, status routines, and escalation paths for truly urgent issues.

17
00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:27.440
Focus blocks should be visible enough that other people understand why attention is protected.

18
00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:33.060
Good scheduling does not worship the calendar; it uses the calendar to defend the work that needs depth.
